          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸ್ವಯಂಸೇವಕ — svayaṃsēvaka — \"a volunteer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನೂರಾರು ಸ್ವಯಂಸೇವಕರು ಸಂತ್ರಸ್ತರಿಗೆ ಊಟ ತಂದರು. nūrāru svayaṃsēvakaru santrastarige ūṭa tandaru. Hundreds of volunteers brought food to the victims."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಸ್ವಯಂಸೇವಕರು, svayaṃsēvakaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸ್ವಯಂ, oneself, and ಸೇವಕ, one who serves: one who serves of his own will."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸ್ವಯಂಸೇವಕ (svayaṃsēvaka) is borrowed from Sanskrit, a modern compound of svayam, \"self, spontaneously\" (CDIAL 13906), and sevaka, \"one who serves\" (Monier-Williams)."
